   "p": "Embryo freezing refers to a procedure that allows people to store their embryos for future use. In this procedure, the embryos are frozen and stored for later use. It involves IVF, a process in which eggs are removed from the ovary of a woman and is then combined with sperm in the laboratory for developing embryos. The embryos are first frozen, thawed, and then placed in the uterus of a woman. Typically, embryo freezing is a type of fertility preservation and may be useful for those women who are struggling with cancer and want to have their biological children after having chemotherapy, radiation therapy, or other surgeries which may lead to infertility. The procedure of embryo freezing is also called embryo cryopreservation of embryo banking. If you want to get your embryos frozen and preserve your fertility for future, consult Dr. Chandana Veeramachaneni, an Infertility Specialist in Vijayawada."
